.TH CSTR_SPLIT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cstr_split \- split the string by a delimiter
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

cstr_split(s, delim, err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro is a pass-through wrapper for cstring_split(). It returns a cvec
of cstr tokens. Each token is its own allocation on the heap.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s      cstr to split
delim  Delimiter string (must not be NULL or empty)
err    Optional pointer to receive an error string on failure
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
cvec of cstr tokens on success, NULL on failure
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The caller must destroy every cstr in the vector. The caller must then
destroy the vector
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_split (3),
.BR cstr_find (3),
.BR cstr_substring (3)
